  "next_source_work": "Complete six-group resource demand collection and pre-effect admission now run within the actual retained resource storage and the existing shared roster owner native call scope. Capacity/snapshot refusal preserves arena/revision; callback failure/SEH/reentry quarantines without rollback. Next bind coherent production package/threshold providers and an executor that consumes the admitted snapshot. Original acquire releases before resolving package/thresholds and cannot be blindly reused as that executor. Route original entries and remaining required readers/writers through the same owner; implement safe reset timing/semantics, embedded asset handoff, service failure compensation and common publication. Two arena-sized heap buffers per call have no game performance validation. Preserve RESET/creation counterexamples. Prioritize fifth-player native admission, FDC140 resource/character creation, control and replication, together with native HUD/identity markers, lobby/loadout, spectating, results/rewards and navigation. Close 1086460 admission, FDCA93 count and 605F28 indirect-tail contracts where required by this path. Deliver a reviewable prototype and bounded runtime plan; validate fifth-player full lifecycle and native UI only with new authorization, then six/eight real independent accounts and clients, then evidence-backed higher capacities. Keep configuration, per-subsystem limits and verified real players separate; current eight-slot candidates are not an architecture ceiling or production support. Do not defer real integration by adding redundant offline cases. No game access without new authorization.",
